Similarly starting with \(f\)1, we can compute \(f\)3 and \(f\)8.

If \(m\) > \(x\), employ the recurrence formula in backward form and write

\[\begin{array}{c}f_{m - 2}(x) = [xf_{m}(x) + x^{2}K_{1}(x) + x(m - 1)K_{0}(x)]/(m - 1)^{2}\end{array}\]

In the latter expression, replace _f_m by _g_m. Fix \(x\). Take \(r\) > \(m\) and assume _g_' = 0. Compute _g_' = 2, _g_' = 4, etc. Then

